verbatim_text:
(1) The right of pre-emption in respect of a property shall be extinguished unless the person claiming or intending to claim its exercise makes: (a) 'Talab-i-Muwathabat' (immediate jumping demand) immediately on receiving the information of the sale in the same sitting or meeting;
(b) 'Talab-i-Ishhad' (demand with witnesses) by sending a written notice under registered cover with acknowledgment due to the vendee within two weeks from the date of knowledge, attested by two truthful witnesses;
(c) 'Talab-i-Khusumat' (demand by suit) by instituting a suit in a Court of competent jurisdiction within the period of limitation prescribed under section 30 (one hundred and twenty days).
